title: For Jeff, in words you can pass on
pid: af65bc6e-dfea-426c-8595-678be6072a1f
body: |2-
  When you type a reply under a message in your unread list (the
  messages under "It subscribes to these." in your copy of my 'to
  Jeff'), saving now files that message in your copy: it leaves the
  unread list, the count beside my note drops by one, and the message,
  with your reply under it, appears at the end of your copy's own
  content, still editable. Before, your reply showed in place but the
  message kept counting as unread, and nothing of yours held your reply.
  The same happens for any edit inside an unread message, a reply to one
  of its questions included. You can then move it into 'maybe done' as
  before. If you ever type a reply in a view of someone else's note, the
  save now warns you that the view will not show it, and that C-c v o
  does.
